<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{% if synthetic %}[SYNTHETIC] {% endif %}UWMC Discharge &amp; Patient Experience Signals</title>
<style>
:root {
  --bg: #fcfcfb; --surface: #ffffff; --ink: #0b0b0b; --ink-2: #52514e; --rule: #e4e3df;
  --accent: #2a78d6; --warn-bg: #fff4e0; --warn-ink: #7a4b00; --bad-bg: #fde8e8; --bad-ink: #8a1c1c;
  --info-bg: #eef4fc; --info-ink: #184f95;
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
    --bg: #1a1a19; --surface: #222221; --ink: #f0efec; --ink-2: #c3c2b7; --rule: #3a3a38;
    --accent: #3987e5; --warn-bg: #3a2c10; --warn-ink: #f3c56b; --bad-bg: #3d1c1c; --bad-ink: #f2a3a3;
    --info-bg: #17263a; --info-ink: #9ec5f4;
  }
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink);
  font: 14px/1.5 -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; }
main { max-width: 980px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 16px 64px; }
h1 { font-size: 26px; margin: 0 0 4px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
h2 { font-size: 18px; margin: 36px 0 10px; padding-top: 12px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
h3 { font-size: 15px; margin: 20px 0 8px; }
.sub { color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0 0 16px; }
.banner { padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 6px; margin: 12px 0; }
.banner.synthetic { background: var(--bad-bg); color: var(--bad-ink); font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px;
  border: 2px solid currentColor; }
.banner.note { background: var(--info-bg); color: var(--info-ink); }
.banner.warn { background: var(--warn-bg); color: var(--warn-ink); }
.tiles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 10px; margin: 14px 0; }
.tile { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px 12px; }
.tile b { display: block; font-size: 24px; }
.tile span { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 12px; }
.table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 12.5px; background: var(--surface); }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align: top; }
th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-2); background: var(--bg); }
td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
code { font-size: 12px; }
.sev { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 3px; }
.sev.failure { background: var(--bad-bg); color: var(--bad-ink); }
.sev.anomaly { background: var(--warn-bg); color: var(--warn-ink); }
.sev.info { background: var(--info-bg); color: var(--info-ink); }
figure { margin: 12px 0; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px; }
figure img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
figcaption { color: #52514e; font-size: 12px; padding: 6px 4px 0; }
ul.tight li { margin: 3px 0; }
.muted { color: var(--ink-2); }
footer { margin-top: 40px; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 12px; }
@media print {
  body { background: #fff; color: #000; font-size: 11px; }
  main { padding: 0; max-width: none; }
  h2 { break-after: avoid; }
  figure, tr { break-inside: avoid; }
  .table-wrap { overflow: visible; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<header>
  <h1>Discharge &amp; Patient Experience Signals</h1>
  <p class="sub">{{ hospital.facility_name }} (CMS facility {{ hospital.facility_id }}) compared with matched national HCAHPS values
  &middot; CMS release {{ provenance.release }} &middot; prepared {{ generated }}</p>
  {% if synthetic %}
  <div class="banner synthetic">SYNTHETIC TEST DATA. Every number in this report comes from fabricated fixture files used to
  test the software. These are NOT actual results for {{ hospital.facility_name }} or any hospital. Do not cite or share.</div>
  {% elif provenance.provenance == "manual" %}
  <div class="banner warn">Source files were placed in the data folder by hand rather than downloaded by this tool, so their
  origin is not recorded automatically. Confirm they are unmodified CMS downloads (checksums are listed under Sources).</div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="banner note"><b>Independent project.</b> This report was produced by an independent, unpaid, open-source tool
  using only public CMS data. It is not an official UW Medicine or CMS report, and UW Medicine did not request, review or endorse it.
  It contains no patient-level data.</div>
</header>

<section>
  <h2>1. Executive summary</h2>
  <div class="tiles">
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ facts.measures_total }}</b><span>HCAHPS rows published for this hospital</span></div>
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ facts.measures_comparable }}</b><span>matched to a national value</span></div>
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ facts.top_box_above_national }} / {{ facts.top_box_below_national }}</b><span>top-box measures above / below national</span></div>
    <div class="tile"><b>{{ facts.data_quality.failure }} / {{ facts.data_quality.anomaly }}</b><span>data-quality failures / anomalies</span></div>
  </div>
  {% for p in summary.paragraphs %}<p>{{ p }}</p>{% endfor %}
  <p class="muted">Narrative method: {{ summary.method }}. Draft for human review before any use.</p>
  {% if summary.problems %}
  <div class="banner warn">The optional AI draft was rejected because it contained unverified content:
    {{ summary.problems | join("; ") }}. The deterministic summary is shown instead.</div>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>2. Focus: discharge and care transitions</h2>
  <p>HCAHPS items closest to the hand-off from hospital to home: discharge information, communication about medicines,
  care coordination and information about symptoms. These describe what patients <em>reported</em>; they cannot show
  whether a discharge was safe or whether a patient understood their medicines.</p>
  {% if charts.focus %}
  <figure><img alt="Dot chart of UWMC versus national favorable responses for discharge and care-transition measures; values are in the table below." src="data:image/png;base64,{{ charts.focus }}">
  <figcaption>Blue: UWMC. Gray: national. Favorable-response measures only. Where only a blue dot shows, the two values are equal.</figcaption></figure>
  {% endif %}
  {% if focus|length %}
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Response</th><th class="num">UWMC</th><th class="num">National</th><th class="num">Gap (pp)</th><th class="num">Favorable gap</th><th>Status</th></tr>
    {% for r in focus.itertuples() %}
    <tr><td>{{ r.domain }}</td><td><code>{{ r.hcahps_measure_id }}</code></td><td>{{ r.hcahps_answer_description or r.hcahps_question }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.uwmc_percent|pct }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.national_percent|pct }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.gap_pp|pp }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.favorable_gap_pp|pp }}</td>
      <td>{% if r.retired_measure %}Retired from the updated survey; reference only{% elif r.comparable %}{{ r.direction_meaning }}{% else %}Not comparable: {{ r.not_comparable_reason }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table></div>
  {% else %}
  <p>No discharge or care-transition measures were published for this facility in this release.</p>
  {% endif %}
  <p class="muted">CMS updated the HCAHPS survey for discharges from 1 January 2025: Care Transition was dropped and Care Coordination,
  Information About Symptoms and Restfulness of the Hospital Environment were added. Results from different survey versions are not compared over time.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>3. Hospital identity and data</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <tr><th>CMS facility ID</th><td>{{ hospital.facility_id }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Facility name (CMS)</th><td>{{ hospital.facility_name }}</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Location</th><td>{{ hospital.address }} {{ hospital.city_town }}, {{ hospital.state }} {{ hospital.zip_code }}</td></tr>
    {% if hospital.hospital_type %}<tr><th>Hospital type</th><td>{{ hospital.hospital_type }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if hospital.hospital_ownership %}<tr><th>Ownership</th><td>{{ hospital.hospital_ownership }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if hospital.hospital_overall_rating %}<tr><th>CMS overall star rating</th><td>{{ hospital.hospital_overall_rating }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    <tr><th>HCAHPS reporting window(s)</th><td>{{ windows | join("; ") or "none" }}</td></tr>
    {% if previous %}<tr><th>Prior release compared</th><td>{{ previous.release }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
  </table></div>
  <p class="muted">Identity verified against CMS Hospital General Information: facility ID, name, state and city must all match
  the expected record or the tool stops. Results cover only what CMS publishes under this one facility ID; other UW Medicine
  facilities are not combined.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>4. Noteworthy descriptive signals</h2>
  {% if signals|length %}
  <p>Ranked by the transparent score in section 9. A gap is the hospital percentage minus the national percentage, in percentage points (pp).</p>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <tr><th>#</th><th>Measure</th><th>Domain</th><th>Response</th><th class="num">UWMC</th><th class="num">National</th><th class="num">Gap (pp)</th><th>Band</th><th>Confidence</th><th>Prior release</th><th class="num">Score</th></tr>
    {% for s in signals.head(8).itertuples() %}
    <tr><td>{{ s.rank }}</td><td><code>{{ s.hcahps_measure_id }}</code></td><td>{{ s.domain }}</td><td>{{ s.hcahps_answer_description or s.hcahps_question }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ s.uwmc_percent|pct }}</td><td class="num">{{ s.national_percent|pct }}</td><td class="num">{{ s.gap_pp|pp }}</td>
      <td>{{ s.gap_band }}{% if s.within_rounding %} (within rounding){% endif %}</td><td>{{ s.confidence }}</td><td>{{ s.persistence }}</td><td class="num">{{ "%.2f"|format(s.score) }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table></div>
  {% else %}
  <p>No top-box measure was comparable, so no signals are ranked.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>5. National benchmark comparisons</h2>
  {% if charts.benchmark %}
  <figure><img alt="Dot chart of UWMC versus national top-box percentages for each comparable measure; values are listed in the table below." src="data:image/png;base64,{{ charts.benchmark }}">
  <figcaption>Each row is one favorable-response (top-box) measure. Blue: UWMC. Gray: national. Where only a blue dot shows, the two values are equal. Values from the table below.</figcaption></figure>
  {% endif %}
  <h3>Favorable-response (top-box) measures</h3>
  {% if top_box|length %}
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Measure</th><th>Question</th><th>Response</th><th class="num">UWMC</th><th class="num">National</th><th class="num">Gap (pp)</th><th class="num">Surveys</th><th>Footnote</th></tr>
    {% for r in top_box.itertuples() %}
    <tr><td><code>{{ r.hcahps_measure_id }}</code></td><td>{{ r.hcahps_question }}</td><td>{{ r.hcahps_answer_description }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.uwmc_percent|pct }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.national_percent|pct }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.gap_pp|pp }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.completed_surveys|num }}</td><td>{{ r.uwmc_footnote }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table></div>
  {% else %}<p>None comparable.</p>{% endif %}

  {% if other_comparable|length %}
  <h3>Other comparable response categories</h3>
  <p class="muted">Middle and bottom response boxes. For bottom-box measures a <em>negative</em> gap means fewer unfavorable
  responses than nationally. "Favorable gap" applies that direction for you.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Measure</th><th>Response</th><th>Direction</th><th class="num">UWMC</th><th class="num">National</th><th class="num">Gap (pp)</th><th class="num">Favorable gap</th></tr>
    {% for r in other_comparable.itertuples() %}
    <tr><td><code>{{ r.hcahps_measure_id }}</code></td><td>{{ r.hcahps_answer_description or r.hcahps_question }}</td><td>{{ r.direction_meaning }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.uwmc_percent|pct }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.national_percent|pct }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.gap_pp|pp }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.favorable_gap_pp|pp }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table></div>
  {% endif %}

  <h3>Not comparable ({{ not_comparable|length }})</h3>
  {% if not_comparable|length %}
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Measure</th><th>Reported value</th><th>Reason excluded from comparison</th></tr>
    {% for r in not_comparable.itertuples() %}
    <tr><td><code>{{ r.hcahps_measure_id }}</code></td><td>{{ r.uwmc_value_raw }}</td><td>{{ r.not_comparable_reason }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table></div>
  {% else %}<p>None.</p>{% endif %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>6. Changes between releases</h2>
  {% if trends is none %}
  <p>No prior release was supplied, so no change over time is reported. A single release cannot show a trend.
  Archived CMS releases are available at <a href="{{ archive_url }}">{{ archive_url }}</a>; see the README for how to add one.</p>
  {% else %}
  {% if charts.trend %}
  <figure><img alt="Dot chart of UWMC top-box percentages in the current and prior release; values are listed in the table below." src="data:image/png;base64,{{ charts.trend }}">
  <figcaption>Dark blue: current release. Light blue: prior release.</figcaption></figure>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="banner warn">HCAHPS results are rolling four-quarter windows. When windows overlap, the two releases share patients,
  so the change is not between independent periods.</div>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Measure</th><th>Prior window</th><th>Current window</th><th class="num">Prior</th><th class="num">Current</th><th class="num">Change (pp)</th><th class="num">National change</th><th class="num">Gap change</th><th>Windows / reason</th></tr>
    {% for r in trends.itertuples() %}
    <tr><td><code>{{ r.hcahps_measure_id }}</code></td><td>{{ r.previous_window }}</td><td>{{ r.current_window }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.previous_percent|pct }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.current_percent|pct }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.change_pp|pp }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ r.national_change_pp|pp }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.gap_change_pp|pp }}</td>
      <td>{% if r.comparable %}{{ r.window_relation }}{% else %}{{ r.not_comparable_reason }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table></div>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>7. Data-quality findings</h2>
  <p class="muted"><span class="sev failure">failure</span> confirmed problem, rows excluded &nbsp;
  <span class="sev anomaly">anomaly</span> possible problem, rows kept and flagged &nbsp;
  <span class="sev info">info</span> context only</p>
  {% if findings|length %}
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Severity</th><th>Dataset</th><th>Check</th><th>Detail</th><th class="num">Count</th><th>Measures</th></tr>
    {% for f in findings.itertuples() %}
    <tr><td><span class="sev {{ f.severity }}">{{ f.severity }}</span></td><td>{{ f.dataset }}</td><td><code>{{ f.check }}</code></td>
      <td>{{ f.detail }}</td><td class="num">{{ f.count }}</td><td><code>{{ f.measure_ids | replace(";", " ") }}</code></td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table></div>
  {% else %}<p>No findings.</p>{% endif %}
</section>

<section>
  <h2>8. Limitations</h2>
  <ul class="tight">
    <li>Differences are descriptive. CMS publishes adjusted, whole-number percentages without standard errors, so no statistical significance is claimed or computed.</li>
    <li>A gap of about 1 pp can be produced by rounding alone.</li>
    <li>HCAHPS covers a sample of adult inpatients who returned a survey; it does not describe every patient or every service.</li>
    <li>National values are averages over all reporting hospitals, which differ in size, case mix and mission from an academic medical center.</li>
    <li>Results reflect a reporting window that ends months before publication.</li>
    <li>Directionality comes from CMS measure-ID conventions; IDs outside those rules are shown but not interpreted.</li>
    <li>Nothing here identifies causes or recommends clinical action.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>9. Methodology</h2>
  <ul class="tight">
    <li>A hospital measure is <b>comparable</b> only when its value is numeric and within 0-100, exactly one valid national row exists with the same measure ID, both cover the identical reporting window, and the response category text matches.</li>
    <li>Gap (pp) = UWMC % &minus; national %. Favorable gap flips the sign for bottom-box measures.</li>
    <li>Gap bands: large &ge; {{ rules.gap_bands_pp.large }} pp, moderate &ge; {{ rules.gap_bands_pp.moderate }} pp, otherwise small. These are reading aids, not significance thresholds.</li>
    <li>Confidence: <i>low</i> with CMS footnote 6 or 10 or fewer than 100 completed surveys; <i>caution</i> with any other footnote or fewer than 300 surveys; otherwise <i>standard</i>. Weights {{ rules.confidence_weights }}.</li>
    <li>Signal score = |favorable gap| &times; confidence weight + 1.0 if, since a comparable prior release, the gap to national grew by more than 1 pp in the same direction. Only top-box measures are ranked, so complementary boxes of one question are not counted twice.</li>
  </ul>
  <details><summary>Directionality rules (first match wins)</summary>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table><tr><th>Measure-ID pattern</th><th>Direction</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
    {% for r in rules.direction_rules %}<tr><td><code>{{ r.pattern }}</code></td><td>{{ r.direction }}</td><td>{{ r.meaning }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
    </table></div>
  </details>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>10. Sources</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Dataset</th><th>CMS ID</th><th>CMS modified</th><th>Retrieved</th><th>SHA-256 (first 16)</th></tr>
    {% for ds, rec in sources %}
    <tr><td><a href="{{ ds.landing_page }}">{{ rec.title or ds.title }}</a></td><td>{{ ds.dataset_id }}</td>
      <td>{{ rec.cms_modified or "not recorded" }}</td><td>{{ rec.retrieved_at or rec.file_modified or "not recorded" }}</td>
      <td><code>{{ (rec.sha256 or "")[:16] }}</code></td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table></div>
  <p class="muted">Provenance: {{ provenance.provenance }}. Data folder: <code>{{ provenance.path }}</code>.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>11. Reproduce this report</h2>
<pre><code>pip install -e .
uwmc-monitor fetch            # downloads the current CMS release into data/raw/&lt;date&gt;/
uwmc-monitor run              # validate, analyze, write output/
uwmc-monitor run --previous-dir data/raw/&lt;earlier-date&gt;   # add a release comparison</code></pre>
</section>

<footer>Generated by uwmc-quality-signal-monitor {{ version }} (MIT licensed). Independent project; not affiliated with or endorsed by UW Medicine or CMS.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
